# badger3000 — environment
#
# One set of names for both stacks. The Astro app in `apps/web` is the future;
# the Next.js app at the repo root still serves production until the cutover, so
# it reads the same `PUBLIC_*` values and falls back to the legacy `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`
# names. Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Astro reads `apps/web/.env`; put the PUBLIC_* block there too (or symlink).
#
# Sanity project id: https://sanity.io/manage → your project → API
#   Sanity            — PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID
#   Sanity (API)      — PUBLIC_SANITY_API_VERSION (pinned so a Sanity API bump
#                       cannot change a deployed build)

# ---- Sanity ----------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production
PUBLIC_SANITY_API_VERSION=2024-03-09
# Optional: draft preview locally. The CDN never serves drafts. Server-only.
SANITY_API_TOKEN=
# Sanity Studio reads these itself; fall back to the PUBLIC_* values above.
# SANITY_STUDIO_API_PROJECT_ID=
# SANITY_STUDIO_API_DATASET=

# ---- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://badger3000.com

# ---- Contact form (ADR 0003) ----------------------------------------------
# Server-only secrets:
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# OWNER_EMAIL=
# CONTACT_FORM_EMAIL=
# RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=
# PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
# Author name for the RSS feed:
# PUBLIC_AUTHOR_NAME=

# ---- Legacy (Next.js) ------------------------------------------------------
# Still honoured while the Next app is live; drop them at the cutover.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTHOR_NAME=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=